    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(s,k\\) and work on a successful selected fit.  The compact support of \\(K\\), fixed \\(r,d\\), and the declared selected-Gram threshold imply\n\\[\n\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}\\le Cn_sTh_{sk}^d,\\qquad\n\\lambda_{\\min}(G_{sk})\\ge cn_sTh_{sk}^d,\n\\qquad\n\\sup_{w_{stk}>0}\\|b_r(u_{stk})\\|_2\\le C.\n\\]\nThe first two inequalities are exactly the upper local-mass bound and normalized lower-eigenvalue test used by the finite dyadic selection rule.  Cauchy--Schwarz and \\(G_{sk}=\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}b_r(u_{stk})b_r(u_{stk})^\\top\\) give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{t,i}|a_{stik}|\n&\\le\n\\left(\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}\\right)^{1/2}\n\\left\\{\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}\n\\bigl(e_0^\\top G_{sk}^{-1}b_r(u_{stk})\\bigr)^2\\right\\}^{1/2}\\\\\n&=\n\\left\\{\\left(\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}\\right)\ne_0^\\top G_{sk}^{-1}e_0\\right\\}^{1/2}\n\\le C.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe covariates and hence \\(a_{stik}\\) do not depend on \\(i\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n\\sum_t|a_{stik}|\\le \\frac C{n_s},\\qquad\n\\sum_t|\\bar a_{sti}|\n\\le\\frac1{K_D}\\sum_k\\sum_t|a_{stik}|\n\\le\\frac C{n_s}.\n\\]\nAfter squaring and summing over the \\(n_s\\) units,\n\\[\n\\sum_s\\sum_i\\left[\\pi_s\\sum_t|\\bar a_{sti}|\\right]^2\n\\le C\\sum_s\\frac{\\pi_s^2}{n_s}=CR_{\\mathrm{tr}}.\n\\]\nThis argument uses the selected Gram itself and therefore does not require \\(Th_s^d\\to\\infty\\).\n\nWe next control the selected radii.  The density lower bound, interior condition, fixed polynomial dimension, and geometric beta-mixing bound imply, for every \\(v\\ge0\\),\n\\[\nP\\{h_{sk}>2^vh_s\\mid E_0,\\widetilde z_{sk}\\}\n\\le C\\exp\\{-cT(2^vh_s)^d\\}\n\\]\nuntil \\(2^vh_s\\ge1\\); at the terminal grid value the failure probability is at most \\(Ce^{-cT}\\).  To see the displayed bound, place \\(q_r\\) disjoint fixed-shape subcubes inside the kernel window.  Each has conditional mass at least \\(ch^d\\).  Expanding the probability that a subcube is missed into successive conditional blocks and using \\(\\sum_{\\ell\\ge1}\\beta_0\\rho_0^\\ell<\\infty\\) gives \\(C\\exp(-cTh^d)\\); occupation of all subcubes makes the fixed-dimensional monomial Gram uniformly positive.  Integration of this dyadic tail yields, for every fixed \\(a>0\\),\n\\[\n\\mathbb E[h_{sk}^a\\mathbf1_{\\mathrm{good}}\\mid E_0,\\widetilde z_{sk}]\n\\le C\\{h_s^a+T^{-a/d}\\},\n\\qquad\nP(\\mathrm{bad}\\mid E_0)\\le Ce^{-cT}.\n\\]\nBecause \\(R_\\star\\ge R_{\\mathrm{sp}}=T^{-2\\lambda/d}\\), the last term is at most \\(CR_\\star\\) for all large \\(T\\).  Empty donor complements and \\(\\max_k\\delta_k>\\delta_0\\) are absent eventually since \\(K_D,D\\) are fixed and \\(m_k\\asymp N\\); all other bad events are ruled out by the finite grid and spectral clipping construction.\n\nPolynomial reproduction follows directly from invertibility:\n\\[\n\\sum_{t,i}a_{stik}b_r(u_{stk})^\\top\n=e_0^\\top G_{sk}^{-1}G_{sk}=e_0^\\top.\n\\]\nTaylor's formula in the maintained Holder convention therefore gives\n\\[\n\\left|\n\\sum_{t,i}a_{stik}m_s(X_{st})-m_s(\\widetilde z_{sk})\n\\right|\n\\le C_{r,d}L\\sum_{t,i}|a_{stik}|\n\\|X_{st}-\\widetilde z_{sk}\\|_2^\\lambda.\n\\]\nSumming with weights \\(\\pi_s/K_D\\) is precisely \\(A_L\\).  The preceding \\(\\ell_1\\) bound and bandwidth moment bound yield\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbb E[A_L^2\\mathbf1_{\\mathrm{good}}\\mid E_0]\n&\\le C\\sum_s\\pi_s^2\n\\left\\{(Tn_s)^{-2\\lambda/(2\\lambda+d)}\n+T^{-2\\lambda/d}+N^{-\\lambda}\\right\\}\\\\\n&\\le C\\{R_{\\mathrm{sm}}\\vee R_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\vee R_{\\mathrm{don}}\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nHere fixed \\(S\\) and fixed positive \\(\\pi_s\\) make the \\(\\ell_1\\) and \\(\\ell_2\\) cohort aggregations equivalent up to a fixed constant, and \\(N^{-\\lambda}\\le N^{-\\kappa}\\).\n\nFinally let\n\\[\n\\Delta_k=\n\\left\\|\\Sigma^{-1/2}\n\\{\\operatorname{vec}((\\widetilde z_{sk})_{s=1}^{S})-z_0\\}\\right\\|_2.\n\\]\nEuclidean projection and \\(c_\\Sigma I\\preceq\\Sigma\\preceq C_\\Sigma I\\) imply\n\\[\n\\Delta_k\\le\n\\sqrt{\\frac{C_\\Sigma}{c_\\Sigma}}\n\\left\\|\\frac1{m_k}\\sum_{j\\notin k}Y_j\\right\\|_2.\n\\]\nIndependence, centering, and \\(\\mathbb E[Y_jY_j^\\top\\mid E_0]=I_D\\) give\n\\[\n\\mathbb E[\\Delta_k^2\\mid E_0]\\le\\frac C{m_k}.\n\\]\nOn \\(\\{\\Delta_k\\le\\delta_0\\}\\), the upper local modulus bounds the weighted surface displacement by \\(C_{\\mathrm{mod}}\\Delta_k^\\kappa\\); on its complement bounded wealth and Markov's inequality apply.  Since \\(0<\\kappa\\le1\\), Jensen's inequality gives\n\\[\n\\mathbb E\\!\\left[\n\\min\\{B^2,C\\Delta_k^{2\\kappa}\\}\\,\\middle|\\,E_0\\right]\n\\le C m_k^{-\\kappa}.\n\\]\nA fixed-fold average and Cauchy--Schwarz now give \\(CR_{\\mathrm{don}}\\).  This proves every assertion.",
